{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $217$ | $234$ | $268$ | $336$ | $478$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a backward difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x)-g(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{g(2)-g(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2)-g(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{268-234}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{1} \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-72065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["