"field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-343779" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343779" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.75$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $6$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.75$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{f}^{′}(0.75)≈$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=0.75.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.25.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.75) & ≈\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.75-0.25)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.75)-f(0.5)}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{0.25} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-343782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343782" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A distance function $s(t)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.02$ | $0.04$ | $0.06$ | $0.08$ | $0.10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $5$ | $9$ | $13$ | $18$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity ${s}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=0.06$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\,\\,{s}^{′}(0.06)≈$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t)-s(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=0.06.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=0.02.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(0.06) & ≈\\frac{s(0.06)-s(0.06-0.02)}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(0.06)-s(0.04)}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{0.02} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.02} \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-343788" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-343788" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "200"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.9$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.9$ |\n\nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a backward difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case, $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{f(-1)-f(-1-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(-1)-f(-2)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1-0.4}{1} \\\\  & =-0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.3"] ["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/a93150906c0681b8654370267fb918076338fa8ab5bf68f50a0062a4ab34af1d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x)-f(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ Applying the above formula with $x=-1$ and $h=2$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{f(-1)-f(-1-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(-1)-f(-3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-(-2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/state.json" "file_sha256" "dbf6bf149064828b1103a4eaae2d31d5202af35460c979b14b79804719118946"} {"question" "q-72067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ab0127b09326b9480bb2e64a6004f0af49145c47f990fb6b62f8576df40bcd6"} {"question" "q-72067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Develope